IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cla-core`
IMPORT `cla-damages`

-- Civil Liability Act 2002 (NSW) -- worked cases for every exported question in cla-core.l4 (s 3B) and cla-damages.l4
-- (Part 2). Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output.
-- Each assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Average weekly earnings figures
-- ($1,900 and $1,800) and the indexed s 16 maximum ($712,000) used here are ILLUSTRATIVE, not the Statistician's or the
-- Minister's real figures.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases -- s 3B and Part 2`

`general` MEANS `negligence, or another claim for death or personal injury not listed here`
`intent` MEANS `an intentional act the defendant did meaning to injure or kill`
`sexual` MEANS `sexual assault or other sexual misconduct by the defendant`
`vicarious` MEANS `vicarious liability for someone else's intentional act or sexual misconduct`
`dust` MEANS `a dust disease claim of the kind brought in the Dust Diseases Tribunal`
`tobacco` MEANS `injury or death from smoking or other use of tobacco products`
`MAIA` MEANS `a motor accident claim under the Motor Accident Injuries Act 2017`
`MACA` MEANS `a motor accident claim under the Motor Accidents Compensation Act 1999 or the Motor Accidents Act 1988`
`work damages` MEANS `work injury damages against an employer under Division 3 of Part 5 of the Workers Compensation Act 1987`
`statutory` MEANS `statutory compensation or a statutory benefit`

`P1A core` MEANS `Part 1A Divisions 1 to 4 and 8: negligence, causation, obvious and inherent risks, contributory negligence`
`P1A other` MEANS `Part 1A Divisions 5 to 7: recreational activities, professional negligence, non-delegable duties`
`P1B` MEANS `Part 1B: liability of organisations for child abuse`
`P1C` MEANS `Part 1C: setting aside child abuse settlements`
`s15` MEANS `section 15: gratuitous attendant care`
`s15A` MEANS `section 15A: gratuitous attendant care in dust disease claims`
`s15B` MEANS `section 15B: loss of capacity to provide domestic services to dependants`
`s15C` MEANS `section 15C: lost employer superannuation contributions`
`s16` MEANS `section 16: damages for non-economic loss`
`s17A` MEANS `section 17A: earlier awards for non-economic loss`
`Div 7` MEANS `Part 2 Division 7: structured settlements`
`P3` MEANS `Part 3: mental harm`
`s49` MEANS `section 49: intoxication and the duty and standard of care`
`P6 rest` MEANS `the rest of Part 6: no recovery when intoxicated`
`P7` MEANS `Part 7: self-defence and recovery by criminals`
`P8` MEANS `Part 8: good samaritans`
`other Part` MEANS `another Part of the Act`

`so` MEANS `the court has found that it is so`
`not so` MEANS `the court has found that it is not so`
`undecided` MEANS `the court has not decided`

`n/a` MEANS `this section does not apply to my claim`
`open amount` MEANS `the Act does not settle the amount`

`non-economic` MEANS `damages for non-economic loss`
`care s 15` MEANS `damages for gratuitous attendant care under section 15`
`care s 15A` MEANS `damages for gratuitous attendant care in a dust disease claim under section 15A`
`domestic s 15B` MEANS `damages for loss of capacity to provide domestic services to my dependants under section 15B`
`other head` MEANS `other damages, such as past lost earnings or out-of-pocket expenses`

`below threshold` MEANS `no damages for non-economic loss: the severity is below 15% of a most extreme case`
`s 16 n/a` MEANS `section 16 does not apply to my claim`
`s 16 open` MEANS `the Act does not settle the non-economic loss amount`

§§ `s 3B`

-- A negligence claim: the whole Act.
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `general` `s16` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `general` `other Part` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a) sexual assault by the defendant: only Part 1B, s 15B, s 18(1)(c) (and Part 2A); Part 1C is not kept (finding 2).
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `sexual` `s16` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `sexual` `P1B` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `sexual` `s15B` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `sexual` `section 18(1)(c): no interest on damages for loss of capacity to provide domestic services` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `sexual` `P7` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `sexual` `P1C` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (a) an act meant to injure or kill: Part 7 is kept as well.
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `intent` `P7` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `intent` `P3` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Vicarious liability for another's act: settled where (a) makes no difference, open where it does (fork F1).
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `vicarious` `s16` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `vicarious` `P1B` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `vicarious` `s15B` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `vicarious` `P7` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b) dust diseases: ss 15A, 15B, 18(1)(c).
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `dust` `s15A` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `dust` `s15` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `dust` `s16` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (c) tobacco: s 15B, s 18(1)(c).
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `tobacco` `s15B` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `tobacco` `s16` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (e1) with s 3B(2): a 2017 Act motor accident.
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `MAIA` `P3` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `MAIA` `s15B` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `MAIA` `s15C` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `MAIA` `s16` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `MAIA` `Div 7` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `MAIA` `s49` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `MAIA` `P6 rest` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `MAIA` `P1A core` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `MAIA` `P1A other` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `MAIA` `P8` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (d), (e) with s 3B(2): an older-scheme motor accident keeps ss 15B and 15C.
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `MACA` `s15B` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `MACA` `s15C` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `MACA` `s17A` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `MACA` `s16` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (f) work injury damages: only Part 1B.
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `work damages` `P1B` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `work damages` `s16` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `work damages` `P3` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (g), (h) statutory compensation and benefits: nothing.
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `statutory` `P1B` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does this part of the Act apply to my claim` `statutory` `P1A core` EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 12 -- earnings cap`

-- Arguments: kind of claim, gross weekly earnings, average weekly earnings ($1,900: three times is $5,700).
#ASSERT `What weekly earnings can the court count` `general` 3000 1900 EQUALS `the amount is` 3000
#ASSERT `What weekly earnings can the court count` `general` 6000 1900 EQUALS `the amount is` 5700
#ASSERT `What weekly earnings can the court count` `general` 5700 1900 EQUALS `the amount is` 5700
#ASSERT `What weekly earnings can the court count` `general` 5701 1900 EQUALS `the amount is` 5700
#ASSERT `What weekly earnings can the court count` `MAIA` 6000 1900 EQUALS `n/a`
#ASSERT `What weekly earnings can the court count` `dust` 6000 1900 EQUALS `n/a`
#ASSERT `What weekly earnings can the court count` `vicarious` 6000 1900 EQUALS `open amount`

§§ `s 14 -- discount rate`

#ASSERT `What discount rate applies` `general` FALSE 0 EQUALS `the amount is` 5
#ASSERT `What discount rate applies` `general` TRUE 3 EQUALS `the amount is` 3
#ASSERT `What discount rate applies` `sexual` FALSE 0 EQUALS `n/a`

§§ `s 15 -- gratuitous attendant care`

-- Bar. Arguments: kind of claim, hours a week, consecutive months, the court's finding on need. JUST TRUE = barred.
#ASSERT `Does section 15 stop my claim for gratuitous care` `general` 6 6 `so` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 15 stop my claim for gratuitous care` `general` 5 6 `so` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 15 stop my claim for gratuitous care` `general` 6 5 `so` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 15 stop my claim for gratuitous care` `general` 10 12 `not so` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 15 stop my claim for gratuitous care` `general` 10 12 `undecided` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does section 15 stop my claim for gratuitous care` `general` 5 12 `undecided` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 3B: s 15 does not apply to dust disease (s 15A instead) or 2017 Act motor claims; open for vicarious liability.
#ASSERT `Does section 15 stop my claim for gratuitous care` `dust` 2 1 `not so` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 15 stop my claim for gratuitous care` `MAIA` 2 1 `not so` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 15 stop my claim for gratuitous care` `vicarious` 2 1 `not so` EQUALS NOTHING

-- Cap. Arguments: kind of claim, hours a week, average weekly earnings ($1,800: $45 an hour).
#ASSERT `What is the most per week for gratuitous care` `general` 40 1800 EQUALS `the amount is` 1800
#ASSERT `What is the most per week for gratuitous care` `general` 60 1800 EQUALS `the amount is` 1800
#ASSERT `What is the most per week for gratuitous care` `general` 39 1800 EQUALS `the amount is` 1755
#ASSERT `What is the most per week for gratuitous care` `general` 6 1800 EQUALS `the amount is` 270
-- s 15A: the hourly rate "regardless of the number of hours".
#ASSERT `What is the most per week for gratuitous care` `dust` 60 1800 EQUALS `the amount is` 2700
#ASSERT `What is the most per week for gratuitous care` `dust` 40 1800 EQUALS `the amount is` 1800
#ASSERT `What is the most per week for gratuitous care` `MAIA` 10 1800 EQUALS `n/a`
#ASSERT `What is the most per week for gratuitous care` `sexual` 10 1800 EQUALS `n/a`

§§ `s 15B -- loss of capacity to provide domestic services`

-- Bar. Arguments: kind of claim, unborn then, provided before, dependant could not do them, hours a week, consecutive
-- months, the court's finding on need, the dependant already recovered. JUST TRUE = barred.
#ASSERT `Does section 15B stop my claim for lost capacity to care for dependants` `general` FALSE TRUE TRUE 6 6 `so` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 15B stop my claim for lost capacity to care for dependants` `general` FALSE FALSE TRUE 6 6 `so` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 15B stop my claim for lost capacity to care for dependants` `general` TRUE FALSE TRUE 6 6 `so` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 15B stop my claim for lost capacity to care for dependants` `general` FALSE TRUE FALSE 6 6 `so` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 15B stop my claim for lost capacity to care for dependants` `general` FALSE TRUE TRUE 5 6 `so` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 15B stop my claim for lost capacity to care for dependants` `general` FALSE TRUE TRUE 6 5 `so` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 15B stop my claim for lost capacity to care for dependants` `general` FALSE TRUE TRUE 6 6 `not so` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 15B stop my claim for lost capacity to care for dependants` `general` FALSE TRUE TRUE 6 6 `undecided` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does section 15B stop my claim for lost capacity to care for dependants` `general` FALSE TRUE TRUE 6 6 `so` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 15B survives s 3B(1)(a): it bars a sexual assault claim too; not a 2017 Act motor claim; settled for vicarious.
#ASSERT `Does section 15B stop my claim for lost capacity to care for dependants` `sexual` FALSE FALSE TRUE 6 6 `so` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 15B stop my claim for lost capacity to care for dependants` `MAIA` FALSE FALSE TRUE 6 6 `so` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 15B stop my claim for lost capacity to care for dependants` `vicarious` FALSE TRUE TRUE 6 6 `so` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- Cap: the s 15(5) hourly rate whatever the hours. $1,800 / 40 = $45 an hour.
#ASSERT `What is the most per week for lost capacity to care for dependants` `general` 20 1800 EQUALS `the amount is` 900
#ASSERT `What is the most per week for lost capacity to care for dependants` `dust` 50 1800 EQUALS `the amount is` 2250
#ASSERT `What is the most per week for lost capacity to care for dependants` `MAIA` 20 1800 EQUALS `n/a`

§§ `s 15C -- superannuation`

#ASSERT `What is the most for lost superannuation` `general` 400000 11.5 EQUALS `the amount is` 46000
#ASSERT `What is the most for lost superannuation` `MACA` 400000 12 EQUALS `the amount is` 48000
#ASSERT `What is the most for lost superannuation` `MAIA` 400000 12 EQUALS `n/a`

§§ `s 16 -- non-economic loss`

-- Arguments: kind of claim, severity (% of a most extreme case), maximum amount in force.
-- Maximum $350,000: 15% -> 1% = $3,500; 16% -> 1.5% = $5,250, rounded up to $5,500; 17% -> 2% = $7,000; 25% -> 6.5% =
-- $22,750, rounded up to $23,000; 33% -> 33% = $115,500; 34% -> $119,000; 50% -> $175,000; 100% -> $350,000.
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `general` 14 350000 EQUALS `below threshold`
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `general` 0 350000 EQUALS `below threshold`
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `general` 15 350000 EQUALS `damages for non-economic loss of` 3500
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `general` 16 350000 EQUALS `damages for non-economic loss of` 5500
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `general` 17 350000 EQUALS `damages for non-economic loss of` 7000
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `general` 25 350000 EQUALS `damages for non-economic loss of` 23000
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `general` 33 350000 EQUALS `damages for non-economic loss of` 115500
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `general` 34 350000 EQUALS `damages for non-economic loss of` 119000
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `general` 50 350000 EQUALS `damages for non-economic loss of` 175000
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `general` 100 350000 EQUALS `damages for non-economic loss of` 350000
-- An indexed maximum of $712,000 (illustrative): 16% -> 1.5% = $10,680, rounded down to $10,500; 15% -> $7,120 ->
-- $7,000; 18% -> 2.5% = $17,800 -> $18,000; 24% -> 5.5% = $39,160 -> $39,000; 26% -> 8% = $56,960 -> $57,000.
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `general` 16 712000 EQUALS `damages for non-economic loss of` 10500
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `general` 15 712000 EQUALS `damages for non-economic loss of` 7000
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `general` 18 712000 EQUALS `damages for non-economic loss of` 18000
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `general` 24 712000 EQUALS `damages for non-economic loss of` 39000
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `general` 26 712000 EQUALS `damages for non-economic loss of` 57000
-- Not in the Table: a fractional severity (fork F5), or over 100%.
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `general` 15.5 350000 EQUALS `s 16 open`
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `general` 101 350000 EQUALS `s 16 open`
-- s 3B.
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `sexual` 30 350000 EQUALS `s 16 n/a`
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `MAIA` 30 350000 EQUALS `s 16 n/a`
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `MACA` 30 350000 EQUALS `s 16 n/a`
#ASSERT `How much for non-economic loss` `vicarious` 30 350000 EQUALS `s 16 open`

§§ `s 18 -- interest`

-- JUST TRUE = s 18(1) stops interest on that head.
#ASSERT `Does section 18 stop interest on this part of my damages` `general` `non-economic` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 18 stop interest on this part of my damages` `general` `care s 15` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 18 stop interest on this part of my damages` `general` `care s 15A` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 18 stop interest on this part of my damages` `general` `domestic s 15B` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 18 stop interest on this part of my damages` `general` `other head` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 18 stop interest on this part of my damages` `sexual` `domestic s 15B` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 18 stop interest on this part of my damages` `sexual` `non-economic` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 18 stop interest on this part of my damages` `dust` `domestic s 15B` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 18 stop interest on this part of my damages` `dust` `non-economic` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 18 stop interest on this part of my damages` `dust` `care s 15A` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 18 stop interest on this part of my damages` `MAIA` `domestic s 15B` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Does section 18 stop interest on this part of my damages` `MAIA` `non-economic` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does section 18 stop interest on this part of my damages` `vicarious` `non-economic` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does section 18 stop interest on this part of my damages` `vicarious` `domestic s 15B` EQUALS JUST TRUE

§§ `s 21 -- exemplary damages`

#ASSERT `Can I get exemplary or aggravated damages` `general` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I get exemplary or aggravated damages` `general` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I get exemplary or aggravated damages` `sexual` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can I get exemplary or aggravated damages` `vicarious` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Division 7 -- structured settlements`

-- s 23: future loss exceeding $100,000.
#ASSERT `Must the court tell us the proposed award first` `general` 100001 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the court tell us the proposed award first` `general` 100000 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the court tell us the proposed award first` `MAIA` 200000 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must the court tell us the proposed award first` `sexual` 200000 EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must the court tell us the proposed award first` `vicarious` 200000 EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 25. Arguments: kind of claim, I have a lawyer, I propose to negotiate a settlement.
#ASSERT `Must my lawyer advise me about structured settlements` `general` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must my lawyer advise me about structured settlements` `general` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must my lawyer advise me about structured settlements` `general` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must my lawyer advise me about structured settlements` `tobacco` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Must my lawyer advise me about structured settlements` `MACA` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
